      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '

    During its Turn, a Unit has a certain number of <b>Action Points
    (AP)</b>.

    Each action performed during the Turn consumes AP, and once no
    AP remain, the Unit can no longer act and must end its Turn.



    <b>---Movement</b>


    To
    move a Unit under your control to another tile, left-click on an <b>adjacent</b>
    tile. If the Unit has enough AP, it will move to that position.

    Moving to
    an orthogonally adjacent tile (in a cross) costs 1 AP, while moving to a diagonally
    adjacent tile costs 2 AP.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 54a3d28dd6785154fac83f0c31a69b7c, type: 2}
